[Site "Original 1.d4 course"]
[Date "2026.09.04"]
[Round "-"]
[White "White repertoire"]
[Black "Classical ...Bb7 setup"]
[Result "*"]

{ Qc2 supports central play and the queen recapture preserves your pawns. Black exchanges a useful knight but reduces White's control of e4. } 1. d4 Nf6 2. c4 e6 3. Nf3 b6 4. g3 Bb7 5. Bg2 Be7 6. O-O O-O 7. Nc3 Ne4 8. Qc2 Nxc3 9. Qxc3 d6 10. Qd3 f5 { Develop the c1 bishop to f4 or g5 when appropriate. Prepare e4 or d5 only after checking the long diagonal. Watch for: The b7 bishop can suddenly attack g2 after central exchanges. } *

