{ The check has led to an early bishop exchange. You can still use the fianchetto while keeping d4 and c4 in the center. } 1. d4 Nf6 2. c4 e6 3. Nf3 Bb4+ 4. Bd2 Bxd2+ 5. Qxd2 d5 6. g3 O-O 7. Bg2 c6 8. O-O dxc4 9. a4 b5 10. axb5 cxb5 { Castle and develop Nc3. Pressure on the long diagonal can become relevant after central pawn exchanges. Watch for: Do not assume that the missing light-squared bishops make the entire position harmless; ...dxc4 and ...c5 remain important. } *

