{ Exchanging on c5 changes the center and lets Black develop a bishop. Your queen on c2 still helps with central control. } 1. d4 Nf6 2. c4 e6 3. Nc3 Bb4 4. Qc2 c5 5. dxc5 O-O 6. a3 Bxc5 7. Nf3 d5 8. cxd5 exd5 9. Bg5 Be6 10. Rd1 Qb6 { Develop Bf4 or Bg5 when useful, then e3 and castling. Keep an eye on ...d5 as Black's freeing move. Watch for: Do not cling to c5 if Black can recover it with a developing move anyway. } *

