{ The knight route costs time but develops a useful piece. White uses the time to occupy the center. } 1. d4 Nf6 2. c4 c5 3. d5 b5 4. cxb5 a6 5. b6 d6 6. Nc3 Nbd7 7. e4 Nxb6 8. Nf3 g6 9. h3 Bg7 10. a4 a5 { Complete development and compare the value of a4 with improving a bishop. Watch ...e6 against d5. Watch for: The b6 knight can return to c4 or a4. A queenside pawn move may give it a target. } *

