{ White continues normal development instead of trying to defend b6 at any cost. The advanced pawn can be surrendered if protecting it slows the army. } 1. d4 Nf6 2. c4 c5 3. d5 b5 4. cxb5 a6 5. b6 g6 6. Nc3 Bg7 7. e4 O-O 8. Nf3 Qxb6 9. Nd2 d6 10. Be2 Nbd7 { Bring out the bishops and castle. Make Black prove compensation in the center, not in a familiar accepted-gambit structure. Watch for: A pawn far from home is often a distraction. Do not move the queen repeatedly to defend it. } *

