{ This move order is related to the Blumenfeld family. Bg5 develops while retaining central tension instead of treating every ...b5 as a Benko. } 1. d4 Nf6 2. c4 c5 3. d5 b5 4. Nf3 e6 5. Bg5 exd5 6. cxd5 h6 7. Bh4 g5 8. Bg3 Bg7 9. e3 a6 10. Bd3 O-O { Use the Blumenfeld lesson in Booklet 18. Central exchanges and the f6 pin determine the correct continuation. Watch for: Do not apply the 5.b6 recipe when you have not captured on b5. } *

