{ Nbd2 answers the check and supports development. After the central exchanges, e3 opens the f1 bishop without weakening the king. } 1. d4 Nf6 2. c4 e5 3. dxe5 Ng4 4. Nf3 Nc6 5. Bf4 Bb4+ 6. Nbd2 Qe7 7. a3 Ngxe5 8. Nxe5 Nxe5 9. e3 Bxd2+ 10. Qxd2 d6 { Develop Be2 or Bd3 and castle. The bishop pair or central space may offer lasting chances once the tactical phase ends. Watch for: Do not take on e5 with the wrong piece before checking pins and ...Nd3+ ideas. } *

