{ Black returns to straightforward development. The e5 pawn disappears, but White can maintain a healthy position. } 1. d4 Nf6 2. c4 e5 3. dxe5 Ng4 4. Nf3 Nc6 5. Bf4 d6 6. exd6 Bxd6 7. Bxd6 cxd6 8. e3 Be6 9. Nc3 Nf6 10. Be2 d5 { e3, Be2 and castling are priorities. Keep central squares controlled and challenge active black pieces. Watch for: Do not use a sequence from the ...Bb4+ line when the bishop is on d6; the pins differ. } *

