{ Develop while answering the check. The knight recapture on d2 helps cover central squares and avoids needless queen exposure. } 1. d4 Nf6 2. c4 e5 3. dxe5 Ne4 4. Nf3 Bb4+ 5. Bd2 Nxd2 6. Nbxd2 Qe7 7. a3 Bxd2+ 8. Qxd2 Nc6 9. Qc3 O-O 10. Rd1 Re8 { Bring out the f1 bishop, castle, and keep the e5 pawn only when it is convenient. Black's knight adventure has cost time. Watch for: Queen checks on h4 or a5 can combine with a loose piece. Always inspect checks before grabbing a second pawn. } *

