[Site "Original 1.d4 course"]
[Date "2026.09.04"]
[Round "-"]
[White "White repertoire"]
[Black "Blumenfeld declined with Bg5"]
[Result "*"]

{ Bg5 pins the f6 knight and declines to help Black build the ideal accepted-gambit center. e4 supports a useful space advantage. } 1. d4 Nf6 2. c4 e6 3. Nf3 c5 4. d5 b5 5. Bg5 exd5 6. cxd5 d6 7. e4 a6 8. a4 Be7 9. Bd3 Nxd5 10. exd5 Bxg5 { Develop the b1 knight, choose a safe bishop square, and castle. Be alert to ...Be7 breaking the pin before Black strikes centrally. Watch for: The f6 knight may become unpinned after ...Be7. Recalculate captures that relied on the pin. } *

