{ Black addresses the pin without fixing the central pawn structure. White must now choose how to complete development and handle the tension. } 1. d4 Nf6 2. c4 e6 3. Nf3 c5 4. d5 b5 5. Bg5 Be7 6. d6 Bf8 7. e4 bxc4 8. e5 h6 9. Bc1 Nd5 10. Bxc4 Bb7 { e3 or a central exchange may be appropriate. Check ...exd5 and ...bxc4 before making a quiet move. Watch for: Do not pretend the pin still prevents ...Nxd5 after the bishop has moved to e7. } *

