{ Ba3 challenges the good d6 bishop. The knight recapture develops a piece that may head toward c2 and e5. } 1. d4 f5 2. g3 Nf6 3. Bg2 e6 4. Nf3 d5 5. O-O Bd6 6. c4 c6 7. b3 O-O 8. Ba3 Bxa3 9. Nxa3 Qe7 10. Nc2 Nbd7 { Use e5 as an outpost and improve the remaining bishop. Keep ...Ne4 and ...g5 under observation. Watch for: Do not put a knight on e5 if exchanging it would strengthen Black's attack or create a protected passed pawn. } *

