{ Qc2 supports central play and questions the advanced knight. Black has a flexible center rather than a Stonewall. } 1. d4 f5 2. g3 Nf6 3. Bg2 e6 4. Nf3 Be7 5. O-O O-O 6. c4 d6 7. Nc3 Ne4 8. Qc2 Nxc3 9. bxc3 Nc6 10. d5 Na5 { Prepare e4 or improve the queen bishop. Meet kingside activity by acting in the center when it is sound. Watch for: Do not allow ...Nxc3 to damage your structure without considering the recapture and long diagonal. } *

