{ Accept the pawn and develop. Black's f-pawn move changes the central and king-safety calculation from an Englund Gambit. } 1. d4 f5 2. g3 e5 3. dxe5 Nc6 4. Nf3 d6 5. Bf4 h6 6. h4 Be6 7. Nc3 dxe5 8. Nxe5 Nxe5 9. Bxe5 c6 10. e4 Qxd1+ { Bg2 and castling are the aims. Return a pawn if necessary to finish development and neutralize threats. Watch for: Do not spend tempi defending e5 with a chain of pawn moves while Black mobilizes. } *

