{ The delayed knight move transposes to the fianchetto King's Indian. You have avoided introducing an unrelated e4-opening repertoire. } 1. d4 g6 2. c4 Bg7 3. Nf3 d6 4. g3 Nf6 5. Bg2 O-O 6. O-O Bf5 7. Re1 a5 8. Nc3 Ne4 9. h4 Nc6 10. h5 e5 { Nc3 and e4 are familiar goals. If Black instead chooses ...c5 or ...d5, consult the relevant central structure. Watch for: Do not assign an opening name before Black has committed the central pawns. } *

