{ e3 maintains a flexible center and opens the f1 bishop. The pin deserves attention, but it does not require an immediate pawn chase. } 1. d4 d6 2. c4 Nf6 3. Nc3 e5 4. Nf3 Bg4 5. e3 Qe7 6. Be2 g6 7. h3 Bxf3 8. Bxf3 c6 9. O-O Bg7 10. b4 a6 { Develop Be2 or Bd3 and castle. Challenge the center or bishop only after counting tactical captures. Watch for: If ...Bxf3 doubles your pawns, assess king safety before accepting the structural damage. } *

