{ Nc3 develops while defending the center. After ...Nxe5, Nd5 attacks the queen with tempo and disrupts Black's intended setup. } 1. d4 e5 2. dxe5 Nc6 3. Nf3 Qe7 4. Nc3 Nxe5 5. Nd5 Nxf3+ 6. gxf3 Qd8 7. Bf4 d6 8. Qd4 c6 9. Nc3 Be6 10. O-O-O Nf6 { Continue with useful developing moves and keep the king safe. If Black exchanges on f3 with check, recapture accurately and reevaluate the structure. Watch for: Do not play Bf4 and Qd2 mechanically against queen checks on b4. The queen's path and the b2 pawn matter. } *

