{ The f-pawn exchange leaves Black with an exposed king structure. Bg5 develops and increases pressure against f6. } 1. d4 e5 2. dxe5 Nc6 3. Nf3 f6 4. exf6 Nxf6 5. Bg5 h6 6. Bh4 g5 7. Bg3 Qe7 8. e3 d6 9. Bd3 Qg7 10. Nc3 Bd7 { Use e3, develop the bishops and castle. Look for central opening moves only when your pieces can use them. Watch for: Do not launch a queen raid before bringing out the rest of your pieces. } *

