{ d5 claims space immediately. Nc3 and e4 build the center; you are not required to add c4 to justify playing 1.d4. } 1. d4 c5 2. d5 Nf6 3. Nc3 d6 4. e4 g6 5. Nf3 Bg7 6. Bc4 O-O 7. O-O Na6 8. h3 Nc7 9. Re1 Bd7 10. a4 e5 { Develop Be2 and castle, or use another coherent king setup. If you later play c4, check whether it restricts useful knight routes. Watch for: Do not confuse a recommended practical move order with a statement that 2.c4 is a mistake. } *

