{ d5 gains time against the knight and e4 supports a broad center. Nf3 develops rather than using too many pawn moves to chase the knight. } 1. d4 Nc6 2. d5 Ne5 3. e4 e6 4. Nf3 d6 5. Nxe5 dxe5 6. Bb5+ Bd7 7. dxe6 Bxb5 8. Qh5 Bb4+ 9. Bd2 Bxd2+ 10. Nxd2 Qf6 { Develop the bishops and castle. Exchange centrally if that improves activity or reduces the chance of overextension. Watch for: A sequence of f-pawn and g-pawn pushes can expose the king while Black catches up in development. } *

