{ e4 uses the central space Black offered; Bd3 and Qe2 support it against the b7 bishop and f6 knight. } 1. d4 b6 2. e4 Bb7 3. Bd3 e6 4. Nf3 Nf6 5. Qe2 d6 6. O-O Nbd7 7. Rd1 e5 8. a4 exd4 9. Nxd4 a6 10. f4 Qe7 { Castle and develop the b1 knight without blocking the pieces you need. Be ready for ...c5 or ...d5. Watch for: The bishop on b7 is already aimed at e4. Support the pawn before spending tempi on the flanks. } *

