{ White occupies the center while Black expands on the flank. The b5 pawn does not have to be attacked immediately. } 1. d4 b5 2. e4 Bb7 3. Bd3 a6 4. Nf3 e6 5. O-O c5 6. c3 Nf6 7. dxc5 Bxc5 8. e5 Nd5 9. Nbd2 Nc6 10. a4 Qc7 { Develop Nc3 or Nbd2 as appropriate, then use a4 or central action if it improves your position. Watch for: Do not trade useful central pawns simply to win a flank pawn that cannot be held. } *
